A||N||1||DaveL||ECM Connectors||||6||
Z||000000||DaveL||03-06-2000||02:57 PM||||I was getting constant Code 14 then code 15 on my 87 SE 2.5 DIS (130,000 miles+). The mechanic I've been taking it to said the ecm connector plugs were worn out and sloppy. Well, I found a short in the system, so now all I get are code 14 messages, which means an open in the circuit, since I know it isn't overheating. I want to take out the console and try playing around with the plugs a little while I drive it, spray them with electric contact cleaner etc. How careful do I have to be while doing this? What would happen if I accidentally unplugged one while running? Do you have to have the battery disconnected to take off and/or replace the plugs, or can you just have the ignition off?||||reg||6
Z||000001||theogre||03-06-2000||07:58 PM||||The battery MUST be disconnected durring ECM connector work. Disconnecting one with the engine running could fry the ECM. ||||reg||1
